  "scenario": "An e-commerce checkout service processes an Order containing exclusive OrderLines and tracks its lifecycle using an OrderStatus enum. To stay extensible, CheckoutController depends on a DiscountPolicy interface rather than concrete discount rules like PercentageDiscount.",
  "goal": "Connect all six types to model controller dependencies, interface implementation, line-item ownership, and order status tracking.",
  "learningObjective": "Combine Dependency Injection, Realization, Composition, and Enum Association in a cohesive domain architecture.",
  "hints": [
    "CheckoutController uses both Order and DiscountPolicy transiently during checkout.",
    "PercentageDiscount implements the DiscountPolicy interface, while Order owns OrderLines exclusively.",
    "Connect CheckoutController -> Order (Dependency), CheckoutController -> DiscountPolicy (Dependency), PercentageDiscount -> DiscountPolicy (Realization), Order -> OrderLine (Composition), and Order <-> OrderStatus (Association)."
  ],
  "solutionExplanation": "CheckoutController depends on Order and the DiscountPolicy interface. PercentageDiscount realizes DiscountPolicy. Order composes OrderLines (strict lifecycle ownership) and associates with the OrderStatus enum.",
